---
import { CONTACT } from '../../../site.config.mjs';
---
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap letter">
    <div>
      <p class="prompt">git log --reverse | head -1</p>
      <h2>Built inside a monorepo that runs a dozen services.</h2>
      <div class="signature">
        <img src="https://github.com/LucasPcq.png?size=96" alt="" width="48" height="48" loading="lazy" />
        <div><b>Lucas Picque</b><span>Founder · <a href="https://github.com/LucasPcq">@LucasPcq</a>{CONTACT && <> · <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a></>}</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>I'm Lucas, and I build wtm. The problem came from my day job as an engineer at a startup: a monorepo of two apps, each with a frontend, a backend and a back office, over Docker with several databases. Once AI agents could take several tasks at once, every task needed its own running stack, for me to check the work and for the agent to check it itself.</p>
      <p>It started as shell scripts to create a worktree, copy its <code>.env</code> and run the hooks. The tools I tried stopped at the worktree, so I built wtm as a product of its own, for any team in the same spot. That team now runs part or all of its monorepo in several worktrees at once with it, every day.</p>
      <p>Next is orchestration: wtm starting, tracking and cleaning up one agent per issue. If your team runs agents in parallel and wants to try it, write to me.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
